  "period_note": "CONSOLIDATED (Group) basis, matching this bank's main Q4/annual series (see sources.json reporting_basis). Source: Southeast Bank's own BSEC-mandated 'Evaluation of the Quarterly Financials by the Audit Committee and by the Board' disclosure table, embedded in its annual report (a corporate-governance disclosure most banks answer with a checkbox, but which Southeast Bank answers with an actual Q1/Q2/Q3/Q4 balance-sheet-and-income-statement table for that report's own year, plus a comparative column for the prior year). Balance-sheet line items are the 1 January to 30 September 2023 period-end snapshot (basis reported). Income-statement line items and EPS are CUMULATIVE FROM 1 JANUARY 2023 (\"1 January to 30 September 2023\" exactly as the table's own column header states), not discrete-quarter figures -- flagged via the _cumulative suffix, basis reported, same convention as CITYBANK. Balance-sheet identity (Total assets = Total liabilities + Total equity + Non-controlling interest) holds to within BDT 1m rounding. Cumulative net profit after tax increases monotonically Q1->Q2->Q3 within 2023 (validated; no violation). Cross-checked against the FY2024 report's comparative column: ALL figures for Q1, Q2, Q3 and Q4 match exactly -- the only year in this table's 2016-2024 span with a completely clean cross-check and no restatement of any kind. Q1 2023 shows a cumulative loan-loss provision of -18m (i.e. a small net provision reversal in the first quarter, a genuine discrete event, not an error) before rising to 1,629m by Q2 and 1,841m by Q3. NOTABLE: the Q4 provisioning-catch-up pattern continues -- cumulative net profit fell from 3,005m (9-month) to 2,134m (full year).",
